# docker compose self-hosting stack (deploy/, share-mvp#630) — the bind-mounted PocketBase data
# directory an operator creates locally; never the reference compose/env-template files above.
deploy/pb_data/
# Compose auto-loads compose.override.yaml next to compose.yaml. That is the right place for
# host-specific tweaks (different published ports, an extra service, a non-loopback binding for
# a LAN test) and the wrong thing to share: the reference stack deliberately publishes to
# loopback only, and an operator's local override must never become someone else's default.
deploy/compose.override.yaml

